            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>In the gas-rich atmosphere of Liavara , magically enlarged aeroplankton make up the bottom of the planet's food chain. Beginning as simple filter feeders, many species of plankton were transformed by vibrations from the Dreamers' wordless songs. The thaumacyte is one such organism, having evolved in areas rich with thaumogen gas and growing much larger than typical microorganisms due to occult interference.</p>\n<p>Thaumacytes look like shifting sacs containing iridescent fluid and colorful organelles. A magically reinforced spell membrane allows these floating amoeboids to survive in a variety of environments. After stowing away on unregulated thaumogen mining vessels, some of these unicellular oddities have spread throughout the Pact Worlds. As they feel a particular pull toward powerful magic like the Starstone, many thaumacytes lurk in Absalom Station.</p>\n<p>Most thaumacytes grow to be about 3 feet wide and are usually translucent with a hint of warmer hues, a coloration useful for hiding in Liavara's atmosphere but making them strange and obvious in most of Absalom Station.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Starfinder Absalom Station"
            }
